implementationPlan.description:
Adversarial self-review (load adversarial-self-review) of the three-file diff. Check:
1. Every way sendMessage returns false ends in the warning and never disposes the panel. The four ways are: no ws, state not 'connected', readyState not OPEN, and send throwing. Only true leads to 'Settings saved.' plus dispose.
2. One click produces exactly one user-facing message. dispose() stays idempotent through its disposed flag.
3. A retry after a failed save works, because media/settings.js never disables saveBtn. S7 proves it.
4. The rows must kill these mutants:
   - the panel ignores the result, as today's code does;
   - updateSettings is left void (a connected save then warns, so S1 fails);
   - dispose is kept on the false branch;
   - the info message is shown on the false branch;
   - the warning text is wrong.
5. The UPDATE_SETTINGS payload and S1-S6 are unchanged. Nothing in moe-jetbrains or the daemon changes.
Parity note for the completion summary: JetBrains MoeSettingsDialog.kt:121-134 closes the dialog after MoeCommandSender.updateSettings' ensureConnected() refusal (:25-32 logs and calls onDisconnected). The edits are lost, but it never claims success. That is out of this row's scope, so do not touch moe-jetbrains.
If the review changes any byte, re-run the step-2 gate and cite only that fresh run.
